==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{ety|ru|:inh|orv:слава}}
{{inh+|ru|orv|слава}}, from {{der|ru|sla-pro|*slàva}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|сла́ва}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-слава.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|ru|avə|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|сла́ва|adj=сла́вный}}

# [[glory]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[сла́ва Бо́гу]]!|glory be to God!; thank God!;}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[на сла́ву]]|first-rate; A-one; excellent}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[в|во]] '''сла́ву''' [[победа|побе́ды]]|to the glory of victory}}
# [[fame]], [[renown]]
#* {{quote-song|ru|year=1922|lyricist=Peter Parfenov|composer=Yuri Cherniavsky|title={{w|Po dolinam i po vzgoriam|Partisan's Song}}|url=|album=|text=[[этих|Этих]] [[лет]] [[не]] [[смолкнет]] '''слава''',<br>[[не|Не]] [[померкнет]] [[никогда]]—<br>[[партизанский|Партизанские]] [[отряды]]<br>[[занимали|Занимали]] [[города]].|t=The '''fame''' of those days will never cease<br>Will never dim—<br>The partisan troops<br>Captured cities.}}
# [[repute]], [[reputation]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[дурна́я сла́ва]]|[[notoriety]]; [[ill repute]]}}
# [[rumour]], [[rumor]]
# {{w|Slava watches|Slava}} (Soviet and Russian watches)

